from pathlib import Path
from PIL import Image,ImageDraw
import json,hashlib
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
player=r'''(async()=>{const h=await(await fetch('source-handoff.json')).json(),images={};for(const frame of h.frames)for(const kind of ['raw','codec']){const im=new Image();im.src=kind==='raw'?frame.rawPNG:frame.png;await im.decode();images[kind+'/'+frame.id]=im}let option='look',tick=0,running=false,elapsedMs=0,epoch=0;const clip=()=>h.clips.find(c=>c.id===option),total=()=>clip().frames.reduce((s,f)=>s+f.durationTicks,0);function role(){let end=0;for(const f of clip().frames){end+=f.durationTicks;if(tick<end)return f.frameId}return clip().frames.at(-1).frameId}function state(){return{option,tick,running,elapsedMs,frameId:role(),sourceFrameId:h.frames.find(f=>f.id===role()).sourceFrameId,tickRate:30,totalTicks:total(),nominalDurationMs:total()*1000/30,terminalTick:total()-1,displayStage:h.displayStage,fullWorldCanvas:h.fullWorldCanvas,candidateCanvas:h.candidateCanvas,commonCropOrigin:h.commonCropOrigin,candidatePivot:h.candidatePivot,contacts:[],geometryScope:'image-registration-only',physicalSupportReviewed:false,supportWorld:null,runtimeAdmission:false,sourceUsefulness:'UNKNOWN pending independent review',oneShotPreview:true}}function draw(){for(const kind of ['raw','codec'])for(const bg of ['light','dark']){const c=document.getElementById(kind+'-'+bg),x=c.getContext('2d');x.fillStyle=bg==='light'?'#e5e0cd':'#182a32';x.fillRect(0,0,...h.displayStage);x.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;x.drawImage(images[kind+'/'+role()],...(kind==='raw'?[0,0]:h.commonCropOrigin))}document.getElementById('state').textContent=JSON.stringify(state(),null,2);document.getElementById('tick').max=total()-1;document.getElementById('tick').value=tick}function seek(t){epoch++;running=false;tick=Math.max(0,Math.min(total()-1,Math.floor(t)));elapsedMs=tick*1000/30;draw();return state()}function select(id){if(!h.clips.some(c=>c.id===id))throw Error('Unknown clip');option=id;document.getElementById('option').value=id;return seek(0)}function play(){const e=++epoch,start=performance.now();tick=0;elapsedMs=0;running=true;draw();function step(now){if(e!==epoch||!running)return;elapsedMs=Math.max(0,now-start);tick=Math.min(total()-1,Math.floor(elapsedMs*30/1000));if(elapsedMs>=total()*1000/30)running=false;draw();if(running)requestAnimationFrame(step)}requestAnimationFrame(step);return state()}document.getElementById('option').onchange=e=>select(e.target.value);document.getElementById('play').onclick=play;document.getElementById('tick').oninput=e=>seek(+e.target.value);window.ATTENTION_REPAIR_REVIEW=window.FAMILY_REVIEW={ready:true,select,play,seek,getState:state};draw()})();'''
for species in ['american_crow','white_crowned_sparrow']:
 p=P/species;h=json.loads((p/'source-handoff.json').read_text());(p/'player.js').write_text(player+'\n');w,ht=h['displayStage'];html=f'<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>{species} attention repair source study</title><style>body{{font:16px system-ui;background:#eee9da;margin:24px}}canvas{{image-rendering:pixelated;width:{w}px;height:{ht}px}}table{{border-spacing:12px}}button,select{{padding:8px}}pre{{font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}}img{{max-width:100%;image-rendering:pixelated}}</style><h1>{species.replace("_"," ")} — targeted attention source repair</h1><p>One new native head-attention drawing; exact existing neutral and closed sources reused. Whole-canvas legacy-world sampler, one shared palette/crop, no pose fitting or foot snap. Actual full stage {w} CSS pixels at DPR1; the fractional legacy world extent is preserved with a transparent ceiling margin. Raw source sampling and codec versions are shown separately.</p><select id="option"><option value="look">New head attention — 60 / 18 / 12 ticks</option><option value="blink">Existing closed-eye schedule</option><option value="idle">Neutral-only authored 90-tick hold</option></select> <button id="play">Play once</button> <input id="tick" type="range" min="0" max="89" value="0"><table><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Raw full-stage RGBA</th><th>Shared codec / common crop</th></tr>'
 for bg in ['light','dark']:html+='<tr><th>'+bg+'</th>'+''.join(f'<td><canvas id="{kind}-{bg}" width="{w}" height="{ht}"></canvas></td>' for kind in ['raw','codec'])+'</tr>'
 html+='</table><p>These are authored source clocks. The final sampled tick is held to the full deadline; no generated in-between or whole-body bob is claimed. Source usefulness awaits independent appearance and geometry review. Contacts are empty, physical support is unreviewed and runtime/live admission is false.</p><img src="normal-light-dark.png" alt="Source-normal neutral, existing blink and new attention on light and dark"><p>Enlarged source head and foot diagnostics:</p><img src="head-feet-diagnostics.png" alt="Enlarged head and feet source pixels"><pre id="state"></pre><script src="player.js"></script>';(p/'review.html').write_text(html)
 # Source-derived crops, never browser captures or edits to frame pixels.
 foot=[80,125,145,150] if species=='american_crow' else [58,83,93,99];head=[111,32,165,79] if species=='american_crow' else [65,51,95,77];factor=5 if species=='american_crow' else 8;sheet=Image.new('RGB',(max((head[2]-head[0]),foot[2]-foot[0])*factor*2+40,(head[3]-head[1]+foot[3]-foot[1])*factor+95),'#eee9da');dr=ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)
 for i,role in enumerate(['neutral','look']):
  raw=Image.open(p/'raw-full'/f'{role}.png').convert('RGBA');dr.text((i*sheet.width//2+10,6),role+' raw source crops',fill='#182a32');y=28
  for rect in [head,foot]:
   cut=raw.crop(rect);bg=Image.new('RGBA',cut.size,'#e5e0cd');bg.alpha_composite(cut);big=bg.resize((cut.width*factor,cut.height*factor),Image.Resampling.NEAREST);sheet.paste(big.convert('RGB'),(i*sheet.width//2+10,y));y+=big.height+18
 sheet.save(p/'head-feet-diagnostics.png')
 probes=[];primary=json.loads((p/'current-primary-manifest-reference.json').read_text());f=primary['frames'][0]
 for contact in f['contacts']:
  xy=[round(contact['x']/f['sourcePixelsPerWorldUnit']),round(contact['y']/f['sourcePixelsPerWorldUnit'])];probes.append({'inheritedImageMarker':contact,'roundedWorldComparisonXY':xy,'rawRGBAByPose':{role:list(Image.open(p/'raw-full'/f'{role}.png').convert('RGBA').getpixel(tuple(xy))) for role in ['neutral','blink','look']},'meaning':'Comparison image probe only; not a cross-pose toe correspondence or physical contact claim.'})
 (p/'contact-diagnostics.json').write_text(json.dumps({'probes':probes,'contacts':[],'supportWorld':None,'physicalSupportReviewed':False,'geometryScope':'image-registration-only','interpretation':'Positive alpha alone does not prove toe anatomy, plantar support, pressure or fixed world contact. Independent normal source review determines whether stance changes are acceptable.'},indent=2)+'\n')
 blink=[s['durationTicks'] for s in h['clips'][1]['frames']];(p/'README.md').write_text(f'''# {species.replace('_',' ').title()} attention repair — source proposal

One targeted native edit produced one real head-attention drawing. The exact current neutral source and existing closed-eye source are reused, not regenerated. There were no retries. Exact submitted prompt/reference hashes and arguments were retained before dispatch; the native original, decoded/PNG IDs and return receipt are unchanged. Model and seed are null because unavailable. Historical reference original/prompt and derivation are retained in source-lineage.json and historical-reference/.

All three native canvases use the same explicit pixel-center sampler in preserved legacy world units. One shared 63-color palette and alpha threshold 128, followed by one common transparent-only crop, are declared in source-handoff.json. No body fit, per-pose crop, paint, warp, image translation or foot snap was used. The native originals and raw full-stage RGBA remain intact. The new source ID is proposed immutable decoded evidence and has not been inserted into the global bank.

Normal display stage is {h['displayStage']}; source legacy world extent is {h['fullWorldCanvas']}. Common crop {h['crop']} gives canvas {h['candidateCanvas']} and pivot {h['candidatePivot']}; zero nonzero codec RGBA pixels were discarded. Exact neutral PNG supplies both entry and return. New attention is authored 60/18/12 at30Hz. Existing named blink retains actual primary timing {blink} at30Hz. Proposed neutral-only idle90 is an authored hold, not an active profile change. Blink and look APNGs preserve the codec RGBA tuples and corresponding delays.

review.html exposes ATTENTION_REPAIR_REVIEW and FAMILY_REVIEW ready/select/play/seek/getState. Raw and codec playback appear on light and dark at actual normal world scale. Head/feet crops are source-derived diagnostics, not browser captures. Contact comparison probes are explicitly unbound; contacts are empty, geometry scope is image registration only, support is null and physical support is unreviewed.

Corvid owns actual input5/proposal and normalization checks. Independent reviewers decide source usefulness; neither the export nor completed paperwork grants a useful source slot. SourcePR80 separates producer facts from importer-owned private policy/evidence/reference bindings. No rights, private pins, review decisions, full runtime admission, saved-yard mutation or live acceptance are invented. Remaining output/quality failures will be retained with this bounded attempt rather than automatically retried.
''')
 print(species,'player ready')
